award ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eleanor_Catton\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d41\"},\"ref\":\"d41\",\"snippet\":\" ... Bring Up the Bodies also won the Booker Prize in 2012.\\n\\nHilary Mantel is a U.K.-born historical fiction writer and is one of the few authors to have won the Booker Prize twice. She is the author of 14 books, including A Place of Greater Safety ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.cbc.ca/books/30-books-to-celebrate-30-years-of-writers-company-1.5755144\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d38\"},\"ref\":\"d38\",\"snippet\":\" ... MacArthur Foundation (used with permission)\\n\\nValeria Luiselli was born in Mexico City and grew up in South Korea, South Africa, and India. The recipient of a 2020 Guggenheim Fellowship and a 2019 MacArthur Fellowship, she is the author of the novels Faces in the Crowd, The Story of ... \",\"title\":\"https://artsandsciences.syracuse.edu/english-department/creative-writing-mf-program/raymond-carver-reading-series/previous-raymond-carver-reading-series/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d42\"},\"ref\":\"d42\",\"snippet\":\" ... Instead, she moved to Sydney, Australia, in 1942, where she had lined up a job with another newspaper. That same year she married the budding Australian author D'Arcy Niland (1917–1967), with whom she had been corresponding as pen pals for some years, and whom she had ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.goodreads.com/topic/show/22141667-winners-of-the-miles-franklin-literary-award\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d52\"},\"ref\":\"d52\",\"snippet\":\" ... Booker Prize, the International Booker Prize, PEN America Literary Awards, and the National Book Award.\\n\\nThese awards are highly coveted, being recognized globally by authors alike across all genres.\\n\\nGet a Custom Author Website\\n\\nWe built all of these sites ☝️\\n\\nCategory-Specific Book Awards and Recent Winners\\n\\nFiction ... \",\"title\":\"https://rocketexpansion.com/book-awards/\"}],\"next_step\":\"Inspect navigation; read a relevant page or change the locating clue.\",\"observation\":{\"first_delivered_source_round\":null,\"prior_deliveries\":0,\"query_key\":\"90d3e5986fd27980a80cbdffe1afffcc4e43d8a21b12b3f8077d2f6c03ccfe96\",\"replay_requested\":false,\"result_fingerprint\":\"f9f528ae6da903597d8433ccc590f3a8ae7ed0a8e3076f42285df40bd4efeb1d\",\"semantic_progress\":\"not_measured\"},\"query\":\"International Booker Prize winner born same city another author grew up\",\"view\":\"full\"}]}","role":"tool","tool_call_id":"call_8e1f78de6b3a4a928f7f11a1"},{"content":"I found a very promising lead. Chigozie Obioma's novels \"The Fishermen\" (2015) and \"An Orchestra of Minorities\" (2019) were shortlisted for the Booker Prize and translated into 30 languages. Let me verify this and check the connection. The key insight: \"An Orchestra of Minorities\" (2019) was a Booker contender, and in 2019, the Booker Prize was won by Margaret Atwood and Bernardine Evaristo. Let me check the details.","role":"assistant","tool_calls":[{"function":{"arguments":"{\"ref\": \"d45\"}","name":"read"},"id":"call_7b81ea0cccc94c73a4c2e29f","index":0,"type":"function"},{"function":{"arguments":"{\"queries\": [\"Chigozie Obioma born city grew up biography\", \"An Orchestra of Minorities 2019 Booker Prize shortlist translated 30 languages\", \"Booker Prize 2019 winner Margaret Atwood Bernardine Evaristo\"], \"top_k\": 8}","name":"search"},"id":"call_7e5498ca4bfc4bab8584b02b","index":1,"type":"function"}]},{"content":"{\"action_slot_charged\":true,\"evidence\":{\"document\":\"d45\",\"document_chars\":17355,\"end\":3000,\"kind\":\"raw_evidence\",\"ref\":\"e1\",\"sha256\":\"79767844ce2071fc5dcf3fb0e64d0cade0ba154ef0fc324d0054c1c767e63138\",\"snapshot\":\"90019ca46504785f620ef12f36abae20080c8c3bc7809053339e4beaa4deb2fd\",\"start\":0,\"text\":\"---\\ntitle: ADVISORS\\ndate: 2022-01-01\\n---\\nADVISORS\\n\\nAdvisors\\n\\nProgram Director\\n\\nChigozie Obioma was born in Akure, Nigeria. His two novels, The Fishermen (2015) and An Orchestra of Minorities (2019) were shortlisted for The Booker Prize and have been translated into 30 languages. He has an LA Times book prize, the prestigious Internationalerpris, FT/Oppenheimer prize for fiction, an NAACP Image award and has been nominated for two dozen prizes for fiction. He was named one of Foreign Policy's 100 Leading Global Thinkers in 2015 and served as a judge of the Booker prize in 2021. He is the Helen S. Lanier Distinguished Professor of English and Creative Writing at the University of Georgia, and the program director of the Oxbelly Writers retreat. His third novel, The Road to the Country, was published in 2024.\\n\\nProgram Manager\\n\\nRosie is a production and event manager based in Athens, Greece, with extensive experience in coordinating high-profile film festivals and cultural events. She holds a degree in Communication, Media and Culture from Athens and pursued further studies in Art History in Paris, culminating in a Master's in Culture & Tourism from Université Paris 1 Panthéon-Sorbonne. Her professional experience includes collaborations with cultural organizations and festivals worldwide, including UNESCO in New York, the Rolex Art Festival, Les Rencontres d'Arles Photo Festival among others. Since 2018, she has served as Festival Coordinator and Special Events Manager for the French Film Festival of Greece, and since 2022, she has been the Head of Production for the Athens International Children's Film Festival. Driven by a deep passion for cultural engagement and sustainable tourism, she continually seeks innovative ways to connect communities through the arts. In her free time, she enjoys playing music and gardening.\\n\\nProgram Director\\n\\nChigozie Obioma was born in Akure, Nigeria. His two novels, The Fishermen (2015) and An Orchestra of Minorities (2019) were shortlisted for The Booker Prize and have been translated into 30 languages. He has an LA Times book prize, the prestigious Internationaler Literaturpreis, FT/Oppenheimer prize for fiction, an NAACP Image award and has been nominated for two dozen prizes for fiction. He was a judge of the Booker prize in 2021. He is the Helen S. Lanier Professor of Creative Writing and English at the University of Georgia, and the program director of the Oxbelly Fiction Writers program. His third novel, The Road to the Country, will be published in 2024.\\n\\nProgram Manager\\n\\nKaterina Papanikolopoulos joined Faliro House in 2022 as Manager of Special Projects – a position that evolved into her role acting as the 2024 Oxbelly Retreat, Fiction Writers Program Manager. Following her graduation from UCLA (Summa Cum Laude, Art History), Papanikolopoulos founded the non-profit Athens Design Forum (ADF), a platform that advocates for overlooked and generative design histories interwoven with global labor and migration pa\"},\"executed\":true,\"next_start\":3000,\"ok\":true,\"previously_received\":false}","role":"tool","tool_call_id":"call_7b81ea0cccc94c73a4c2e29f"},{"content":"{\"action_slot_charged\":true,\"executed\":true,\"ok\":true,\"results\":[{\"cached\":false,\"hits\":[{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d45\"},\"ref\":\"d45\",\"snippet\":\" ... 2022-01-01\\n---\\nADVISORS\\n\\nAdvisors\\n\\nProgram Director\\n\\nChigozie Obioma was born in Akure, Nigeria. His two novels, The Fishermen (2015) and An Orchestra of Minorities (2019) were shortlisted for The Booker Prize and have been translated into 30 languages. He has an LA Times book prize, the prestigious ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.oxbelly.com/fiction-writers-program/advisors\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d34\"},\"ref\":\"d34\",\"snippet\":\" ... Farrell\\n*Karen Joy Fowler\\n*Linda Grant\\n*Abdulrazak Gurnah\\n*Sarah Hall\\n*Mohsin Hamid\\n*Shirley Hazzard\\n*Philip Hensher\\n*Mary Lawson\\n*David Lodge\\n*Patrick McCabe\\n*Colum McCann\\n*Tom McCarthy\\n*Shena Mackay\\n*Chigozie Obioma\\n*Michael Ondaatje\\n*Joseph O'Neill\\n*Tim Parks\\n*Caryl Phillips\\n*Julian Rathbone\\n*Mordecai Richler\\n*Arundhati Roy\\n*Bernice Rubens\\n*Donal ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_winners_and_nominated_authors_of_the_Booker_Prize\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d53\"},\"ref\":\"d53\",\"snippet\":\" ... Chigozie Obioma\\ndate: 2000-01-01\\n---\\n-\\n\\n- MajorsMinorsCertificates\\n\\n>>\\n\\n- Policies & ProceduresFYW Guidebook\\n\\n>>\\n\\n- Digital Learning LabsPortfoliosEvaluationsMoran ePortfolio AwardsBarnett Essay AwardsDouble Dawgs\\n\\n>>\\n\\n- Transfer FAQProspective Student Information\\n\\n>>\\n\\n- Study AbroadInternships and Research Opportunities\\n\\n>>\\n\\n-\\n\\n>>\\n\\n- Double DawgsTransfer Student InformationDual Degree Progra\",\"title\":\"https://www.english.uga.edu/directory/people/chigozie-obioma\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d54\"},\"ref\":\"d54\",\"snippet\":\" ... This book brilliantly explores the effects of slavery and colonialism on African families as the story unfolds between West Africa and the United States.\\n\\n- The Fishermen (2015) by Chigozie Obioma (Nigeria): In this heartbreaking tale, four brothers in a small Nigerian town have their lives turned upside down ... \",\"title\":\"https://enkoeducation.com/the-must-read-in-african-literature/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d55\"},\"ref\":\"d55\",\"snippet\":\" ... Appiah argues that, unlike their counterparts who grew up facing the crudest forms of racial and colonial discrimination in the West and the Francophone subcontinent, the likes of S̩óyinká were \\\"children who were extracted from the traditional culture of their parents and grandparents and thrust into the ... \",\"title\":\"https://africasacountry.com/2019/04/why-im-no-longer-talking-to-nigerians-about-race\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d56\"},\"ref\":\"d56\",\"snippet\":\" ... Chigozie Obioma, in The Orchestra of Minorities does the same. You shall notice in my next novel, The Wanderers [to be published in April/May], that I delve into this a little deeper also, to depict the notion of the absurdity of the human condition, which though popularized ... \",\"title\":\"https://africasacountry.com/2021/03/the-xhosa-literary-revival\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d57\"},\"ref\":\"d57\",\"snippet\":\" ... Purple Hibiscus (2003), Half of a Yellow Sun (2006), Americanah (2013)\\n* Chigozie Obioma (Nigeria): The Fishermen (2015), An Orchestra of Minorities (2019)\\n* José Eduardo Agualusa (Angola): Rainy Season, Creole, The Book of Chameleons, My Father's Wives\\n* Ama Ata Aidoo (Ghana): Our Sister Killjoy (1977), Changes: a Love ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/African_literature\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d58\"},\"ref\":\"d58\",\"snippet\":\" ... I, a great new African writer is asking these questions in a spare yet extraordinary novel about this bloody stain on human history.\\\"\\n\\n–Chigozie Obioma (The New York Times Book Review)\\n\\nFinalists:\\n\\nPeter Cameron, What Happens at Night (Catapult)\\n\\nAkwaeke Emezi, The Death of Vivek Oji (Riverhead)\\n\\nDanielle ... \",\"title\":\"https://lithub.com/the-award-winning-novels-of-2021/\"}],\"next_step\":\"Inspect navigation; read a relevant page or change the locating clue.\",\"observation\":{\"first_delivered_source_round\":null,\"prior_deliveries\":0,\"query_key\":\"80b304dfa4e662090e1b65681fc38e71d5a33ea05e613a6ba40dea06863420bf\",\"replay_requested\":false,\"result_fingerprint\":\"023e90c51b104eee9d79c0fc912aa48fb7744e963412940c9a9ae3519bc4b963\",\"semantic_progress\":\"not_measured\"},\"query\":\"Chigozie Obioma born city grew up biography\",\"view\":\"full\"},{\"cached\":false,\"hits\":[{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d45\"},\"ref\":\"d45\",\"snippet\":\" ... His two novels, The Fishermen (2015) and An Orchestra of Minorities (2019) were shortlisted for The Booker Prize and have been translated into 30 languages. He has an LA Times book prize, the prestigious Internationalerpris, FT/Oppenheimer prize for fiction, an NAACP Image award and has been nominated ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.oxbelly.com/fiction-writers-program/advisors\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d34\"},\"ref\":\"d34\",\"snippet\":\" ... Guo *Joanna MacGregor |\\n| 2019 | Shortlist | Lucy Ellmann | Ducks, Newburyport | Galley Beggar | *Peter Florence (chair) *Afua Hirsch *Liz Calder *Xiaolu Guo *Joanna MacGregor |\\n| 2019 | Shortlist | Chigozie Obioma | An Orchestra of Minorities | Little, Brown | *Peter Florence (chair) *Afua Hirsch *Liz Calder *Xiaolu Guo *Joanna MacGregor |\\n| 2019 | Shortlist | Salman Rushdie | Quichotte ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_winners_and_nominated_authors_of_the_Booker_Prize\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d3\"},\"ref\":\"d3\",\"snippet\":\" ... 150px\\n\\nThe Booker Prize, formerly the Booker Prize for Fiction (1969–2001) and the Man Booker Prize (2002–2019), is a prestigious literary award conferred each year for the best single work of sustained fiction written in the English language, which was published in the United Kingdom or ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Booker_Prize\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d44\"},\"ref\":\"d44\",\"snippet\":\" ... Her 2019 translation of Krishna Sobti's A Gujarat Here, a Gujarat There was awarded the Modern Language Association's Aldo and Jeanne Scaglione Translation Prize.\\n\\nIn speaking to the jury's rationale, the panel's chair, Wynne is quoted, saying, \\\"This has been an exceptionally strong shortlist ... \",\"title\":\"https://publishingperspectives.com/2022/05/geetanjali-shree-and-daisy-rockwell-win-the-international-booker-prize/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d46\"},\"ref\":\"d46\",\"snippet\":\" ... 14 of the 30 biggest-selling translated fiction titles in the United Kingdom in 2022 were originally written in Japanese\\n\\n- 1.9 million translated fiction titles, per the report, were sold in the United Kingdom in 2022\\n\\nAgain, our International Booker Prize shortlist report accompanies this one, here ... \",\"title\":\"https://publishingperspectives.com/2023/04/london-book-fair-the-bookers-new-data-on-translation-buyers/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d59\"},\"ref\":\"d59\",\"snippet\":\" ... He has written more than 30 plays, including Namnet (The Name), Vinter (Winter) and Ein sommars dag (A Summer's Day). His longer works include the Septology trilogy, the third volume of which was shortlisted for the international Booker prize in 2022.\\n\\nSeptology, which Fosse started during a ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.theguardian.com/books/2023/oct/05/jon-fosse-wins-the-2023-nobel-prize-in-literature\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d43\"},\"ref\":\"d43\",\"snippet\":\" ... That it was ever even published – earning the first of her two Booker shortlistings, in 2012 – owed to the disillusionment of former Amazon employee Stefan Tobler, now 49, then working as a freelance translator assessing potential foreign-language acquisitions for a large literary imprint. When his proposal to ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.theguardian.com/books/2023/jul/16/uk-indie-publishing-mavericks-shook-up-books-booker-nobel-fitzcarraldo-sort-of-books-daunt\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d60\"},\"ref\":\"d60\",\"snippet\":\" ... As Erigha (2019, 2021) shows, \\\"racial valuations\\\" operate through an interaction between creators' racial identities and the genre categories their works are slotted into. We show that in the construction of the category of postcolonial literature through the Booker Prize (Anand and Jones 2008), non-white authors end ... \",\"title\":\"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC10837049/\"}],\"next_step\":\"Inspect navigation; read a relevant page or change the locating clue.\",\"observation\":{\"first_delivered_source_round\":null,\"prior_deliveries\":0,\"query_key\":\"cb68f1e294f79b9a8d9e4a0d480ed4150540e222d500d8e1282472f3c8e33d02\",\"replay_requested\":false,\"result_fingerprint\":\"2df1e2c2b1090acbadaa537152c6ca2bfcaffbd70f886e4aa6c99ab204912a39\",\"semantic_progress\":\"not_measured\"},\"query\":\"An Orchestra of Minorities 2019 Booker Prize shortlist translated 30 languages\",\"view\":\"full\"},{\"cached\":false,\"hits\":[{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d61\"},\"ref\":\"d61\",\"snippet\":\" ... If you want to understand modern-day Britain, this is the writer to read.\\\"\\n\\nAccolades\\n\\nGirl, Woman, Other was joint winner (with Margaret Atwood's The Testaments) of the 2019 Booker Prize,Flood, Alison (14 October 2019), \\\"Margaret Atwood and Bernardine Evaristo share Booker prize 2019\\\", The Guardian ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Girl,_Woman,_Other\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d3\"},\"ref\":\"d3\",\"snippet\":\" ... Burns | Milkman | Literary fiction | |\\n| 2019 | Margaret Atwood | The Testaments | Literary fiction | |\\n| 2019 | Bernardine Evaristo The Booker Prizes |url= |access-date=2022-09-26 |website=thebookerprizes.com |date=28 May 1959 |language=en}} | Girl, Woman, Other | Experimental literature | |\\n| 2020 | Douglas Stuart The Booker Prizes |url= |access-date=2022-09 ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Booker_Prize\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d62\"},\"ref\":\"d62\",\"snippet\":\" ... Girl, Woman, Other, joint winner 2019 by Bernardine Evaristo This joint 2019 Booker Prize winner follows twelve characters on their personal journeys over the last one hundred years. From Newcastle to Cornwall and the beginning of the twentieth century to the modern day, each of them is searching ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.panmacmillan.com/blogs/literary/our-all-time-favourite-man-booker-prize-winning-novels\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d63\"},\"ref\":\"d63\",\"snippet\":\" ... 9.5\\n\\nGirl, Woman, Other - Bernardine Evaristo (2019) - 9\\n\\nA Brief History of Seven Killings - Marlon James (2015) - 9\\n\\nBring Up The Bodies - Hilary Mantel (2012) - 8.5\\n\\nThe Sense of an Ending - Julian Barnes (2011) - 8\\n\\nThe Testaments - Margaret Atwood (2019) - 8\\n\\nMilkman - Anna Burns (2018) - 8 ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.ontheprize.co.uk/blog/the-booker-prize-in-the-2010s\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d64\"},\"ref\":\"d64\",\"snippet\":\" ... novel premiered in 2017 and was cowritten by Atwood. In 2019 The Testaments, a sequel to The Handmaid's Tale, was published to critical acclaim and was a cowinner (with Bernardine Evaristo's Girl, Woman, Other) of the Booker Prize.\\n\\nThe Blind Assassin (2000) is an intricately constructed ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.britannica.com/biography/Margaret-Atwood\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d34\"},\"ref\":\"d34\",\"snippet\":\" ... Leanne Shapton *Jacqueline Rose |\\n| 2019 | Winners | Margaret Atwood | The Testaments | Chatto & Windus | *Peter Florence (chair) *Afua Hirsch *Liz Calder *Xiaolu Guo *Joanna MacGregor |\\n| 2019 | Winners | Bernardine Evaristo | Girl, Woman, Other | Hamish Hamilton | *Peter Florence (chair) *Afua Hirsch *Liz C